questions.question:
Code in the API process (the OpenTelemetry SDK with the AsyncLocalStorage context manager is started before the app):
// submissions.service.ts, inside the handler of POST /submissions, after the insert
this.scanner.once(`scanned:${submission.id}`, (verdict: string) => {
  this.logger.info({ verdict, submission_id: submission.id }, "scan result");
});

// antivirus.poller.ts, started once at boot
setInterval(() => tracer.startActiveSpan("antivirus.poll", async (span) => {
  for (const r of await this.scannerApi.results()) this.scanner.emit(`scanned:${r.submissionId}`, r.verdict);
  span.end();
}), 250);

Log line:
{"msg":"scan result","verdict":"clean","submission_id":"sub_7c1","trace_id":"9e01c3b5a7d24f6e8b1a0c2d4e6f8a1b"}
(9e01c3b5... is the trace of an antivirus.poll span; the request's trace is 4bf92f35...)

Statement: "The listener logs the poller's trace id because emit() calls it synchronously, in the context active inside emit(), not in the context that was active when once() registered it."

Producer, API process:
await tracer.startActiveSpan("send grading", { kind: SpanKind.PRODUCER }, async (span) => {
  await this.gradingQueue.add("grade", { submissionId: submission.id });
  span.end();
});

The stored job, read from Redis:
{"name":"grade","data":{"submissionId":"sub_7c1"},"opts":{"attempts":3}}

Worker process, started with: node --import ./otel.js dist/worker.js
(otel.js starts the same SDK and context manager as the API.)
new Worker("grading", (job) => tracer.startActiveSpan("process grading", { kind: SpanKind.CONSUMER }, async (span) => { ... }));

Statement: "Both processes run the SDK with the AsyncLocalStorage context manager, so the process grading span already continues the request's trace; the separate root trace the backend shows must be a display problem of the backend."
